 "finding": "The gated reconstruction's depth comes from the pass, not the ground. On the 2022 pass one turn of its fit spans 6.17 m and the scale repeats every 308 to 309 m, so the mirror mostly falls past the 300 m it draws: 4,700 of 4,851 passing positions stand within ten turns of the surface, 151 at the mirror's shallow end. On the 2025 passes, over Giza and over Sacsayhuamán, one turn spans 3.80 m and the scale repeats every 190 m, so the same fits stand twice: 3,002 of 4,650 positions near the surface and 1,647 at the mirror, near 190 m down. One choice, drawn at two levels."
